A||||11||walsh2001||Fiero.... dead again!!!||||9||
Z||000000||walsh2001||06-26-2001||11:28 AM||||Help me with this one guys...<P>My car just died at the nearby high school. <P>Symptoms:<P>Car is parked upward on a hill. I got in and tried to start it... everything came on lights, fuel pump, etc.. but nothing happened.<P>I assumed that the starter had become locked in the flywheel. I therefore put it in reverse so that it would roll backward and release the gear. <P>Instead, the transmission locked up, the clutch went to the floor, and I could not shift out of reverse. I tried pushing the car forward and backward, but it would not budge. With a bit of shaking I was able to knock it out of gear.<P>The Clutch is still out, the car will not start, and it still locks up in whatever gear I put it in. On top of that, the pushrod on the slave cylinder puched its way through the clutch lever on the side of the tranny (it tore the plastic seat out).<P>I am hopelessly lost on this one... the end seems near. I am having it towed. Any help (or sympathy) is welcome. It was working fine up until this point.<P>(note: my fiance noted a popping/spring noise when we were shacking it to get it out of gear, I am not sure what this was)||||reg||9
Z||000001||rogergarrison||06-26-2001||12:55 PM||||my 454 boat did that.......valve broke and wedged between top of head and piston=one blown big block. hope you get off easier. lucky for me, I was sponsored by Jasper Marine engines, they sent a new one.||||reg||1
Z||000002||walsh2001||06-27-2001||12:36 AM||||I may be moving on to a Honda...sniff... car is being towed tomorrow. Anything I can do to save it??<P>P.S. It is the tranny, the rest of the car is in great shape. Will sell for $500||||reg||3
